### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 09 — AUTONOMOUS CRON SCHEDULER
###
### ArcClaw supports scheduling future agent tasks via the cron
### scheduler. Agents schedule tasks via ScheduleTaskTool and list/
### manage them via ManageScheduleTool or zero-token reflexes.
###
### Only coordinator and synthesizer roles can schedule tasks
### (they are the only roles with scheduletask in their tool schema).
### Researcher, coder, debugger, and architect CANNOT schedule.
###
### End-to-end flow:
###   1. User instructs coordinator to schedule a task
###   2. Agent invokes ScheduleTaskTool with:
###        cronExpression (5-field UNIX), goal, timezone, runOnce
###   3. ScheduleTaskTool validates via cron-utils, writes AgentCronEntity
###   4. AgentCronScheduler polls SQLite every 30 seconds
###   5. On fire: CronJobRunner executes agent loop (maxIterations=2)
###      Max-lookback-window: PT5M (jobs older than 5 min not replayed on restart)
###   6. CronResultHandler fires CDI AgentJobCompleted event
###   7. ChannelCronNotificationDispatcher routes result to correct channel
###      (Phase 64-C2: generic dispatcher, not Telegram-specific)
###
### Safeguards in ScheduleTaskTool:
###   - Fork-bomb guard: goal prefixed "CRON:"; nested CRON: rejected
###   - Naked-pronoun guard: vague goals ("it", "this", "that") rejected
###   - runOnce=true → job row deleted after first execution
###
### Audit events:
###   CRONCREATED (mandatory) → job persisted
###   CRONFIRED   (mandatory) → job executed successfully
###   CRONFAILED  (mandatory) → job execution threw an error
###   CRONDELETED (non-mandatory) → job deleted
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw serve mode, GROQ_API_KEY set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-0] Create session for cron scheduling tests
# @name cronSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCHEDULE RECURRING TASKS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-1] Schedule a recurring task (every minute)
# Agent parses "every minute" → cronExpression="* * * * *"
# Expect 200: agent confirms schedule with cron ID
# Audit event: CRONCREATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every minute that answers: What is the current JVM uptime in seconds?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

### [CRON-2] Schedule a one-shot task (runOnce=true)
# runOnce=true → row deleted after first fire
# Expect 200: confirmation with runOnce indicated
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a one-time task to run in 2 minutes that prints: ArcClaw cron job executed successfully.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

### [CRON-3] Schedule with specific timezone
# Expect: timezone=Asia/Kolkata in ScheduleTaskTool params
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every day at 9 AM IST (Asia/Kolkata timezone) that summarizes: Daily health check complete.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LIST SCHEDULED TASKS (zero-token reflex paths)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-4] /crons — list via reflex (no LLM call)
# Expect 200: formatted list of all cron jobs with IDs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-5] /list crons — natural language alias
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/list crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-6] List via ManageScheduleTool (LLM-invoked, not reflex)
# Agent calls ManageScheduleTool with action=list
# Expect 200: same list as /crons
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Using the manage schedule tool, list all my scheduled tasks.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [CRON-6a] Session status check after cron creation
# Expect 200: COMPLETED (cron creation tasks all finished)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [CRON-6b] Schedule via GitHub HITL — cron that uses a tool
# A cron job that internally needs github → scheduler sees AWAITING_APPROVAL.
# Notification arrives via ChannelCronNotificationDispatcher (Phase 64-C2).
# Goal uses CRON: prefix to prevent fork-bomb nesting.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run in 1 minute that lists the public repos of GitHub user rsrini7.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELETE SCHEDULED TASKS
# IMPORTANT: Replace CRON_ID with actual ID from CRON-4 output.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-7] deletecron via reflex — replace CRON_ID with actual value from CRON-4
# DeleteCronReflex matches: input.startsWith("deletecron")
# Expect 200: "✅ Cron job <id> deleted." or "❌ Cron job not found."
# Audit event: CRONDELETED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_CRON_ID_FROM_CRON4",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-8] Delete via ManageScheduleTool (LLM-invoked)
# Coordinator invokes ManageScheduleTool with action=delete, cronId=<id>
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Using the manage schedule tool, delete cron job with ID REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_CRON_ID.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [CRON-9] Delete non-existent ID → "not found" message
# maxIterations=1 — this is a reflex, no LLM needed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron 00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAFEGUARD TESTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-10] Naked-pronoun guard — vague goal rejected by ScheduleTaskTool
# "it", "this", "that", "the result" without specificity → tool returns error.
# Expect 200: agent returns error asking to restate goal concretely.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every hour to do it again.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [CRON-11] Coder CANNOT schedule — empty tool schema
# Brahma has no scheduletask or manageschedule in its schema.
# Expect 200: agent explains it cannot create schedules (no tool available).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every morning at 8 AM to print hello.",
    "agentRole": "coder",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [CRON-12] Researcher CANNOT schedule — no scheduletask in schema
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a daily research task.",
    "agentRole": "researcher",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [CRON-13] Fork-bomb guard — cron job cannot schedule another cron job
# Goals fired by AgentCronScheduler are prefixed with "CRON:".
# ScheduleTaskTool rejects goals that start with "CRON:" (nested scheduling).
# Simulate by sending CRON: prefix explicitly.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "CRON: schedule another task every minute",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WAIT & OBSERVE CRON EXECUTION
# AgentCronScheduler polls every 30 seconds.
# After scheduling CRON-1 (every minute), wait ~90 seconds then verify.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-14] Check audit for CRONFIRED event (run after ~90 seconds)
# Expect: eventType=CRONFIRED in the audit list
# If CRONFAILED appears instead: check GROQ_API_KEY and agent loop logs.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [CRON-15] List crons after one-shot execution — runOnce job gone
# CRON-2's one-shot job should have fired and auto-deleted.
# Expect: the one-shot job no longer appears in /crons.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-16] Verify HMAC chain intact after cron fires
# CRONFIRED is a mandatory event — it must be in the chain.
# Expect: {"valid":true,"brokenAtId":null,"totalRows":N}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/verify
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SYNTHESIZER — also has cron scheduling capability
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-17] Create session for synthesizer cron test
# @name synthCronSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [CRON-18] Synthesizer can schedule cross-domain tasks
# Dattatreya has scheduletask + manageschedule in its tool schema.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a one-time task to run in 1 minute that performs a cross-domain summary: what are the key JVM metrics an AI agent kernel should monitor for memory, throughput, and garbage collection?",
    "agentRole": "synthesizer",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "synthesizer",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLEANUP
# IMPORTANT: Delete all cron jobs BEFORE deleting sessions,
# otherwise every-minute jobs will keep firing after the session is gone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Delete all remaining cron jobs (run /crons first to get IDs, then deletecron each)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Using the manage schedule tool, list all scheduled tasks and delete each one.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
